  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure remains centered over the Mid-\nAtlantic with a coastal trough off the coast. The high is\nsupplying calm winds and clear skies, allowing for areas of\ndense fog to develop. This fog will be around through the AM\ncommute today, and will contemplate a DFA to account for this \nover the next several hours. \n\nHts/thicknesses build further today and temps climbing back to \n~10 degrees above climo with highs upr 70s to near 80 inland to \nlow 70s OBX. A reinforcing back door dry cool front will push \nthrough tonight bringing temps down closer to climo (low 70s \nmost locales) over the weekend. Low temps will also remain above\nnormal through much of the period with readings in the 50s. \nNormal lows for most of the FA are in the 45-50 range now. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...High pres ridge finally begins to break down by\nTuesday and esp Wednesday as next potential low pres area and\ncold front make it's way into the region on active sub tropical\njet. Some convergence on timing with the 30/00Z model suite with\npops inc a bit during the mid week time frame. This system  \nappearsit will finally bring beneficial widespread rain to the \narea.",
